.TH iron-vault-unlock 1  "Iron Vault" "Iron Vault Manual"
.SH NAME
iron\-vault\-unlock \- Open the vault: the service prompts for the vault passphrase, read with echo off or from stdin
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBiron\-vault unlock\fR [\fB\-\-admin\-socket\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open the vault: the service prompts for the vault passphrase, read with echo off or from stdin
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-admin\-socket\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Use the admin socket at PATH instead of this installation\*(Aqs, for example one forwarded over SSH. Every client command takes it; `serve` refuses it, because the service always binds its own installation\*(Aqs socket
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
